  "initial_run": "The first retirement assertion on both platforms assumed the serialized key order of an incomplete JSON response. The corrected peer compares the wire header and validates the payload prefix independently of key order.",
  "limits": [
    "Performance is end-to-end over one local subprocess: 2048 calls per run, closed-loop window 32, three interleaved runs per driver and profile.",
    "The Windows polling driver uses ordinary redirected anonymous pipes. The Windows event driver uses named pipes with overlapped child handles. Linux uses ordinary redirected pipes for both.",
    "The event driver is an example. Automatic process attachment, negotiated deadline/cancellation and native production qualification are open.",
    "Windows and WSL UINT32_BE event P99 show run-to-run spread. These are descriptive short-run samples without a release gate."
